  "known_limitations": [
    "Redis and Celery may redeliver a message; database fencing and unique keys protect the tested business writes but do not prove arbitrary external side effects exactly once.",
    "Automatic outbox recovery creates at most five rows per job, including the initial row. A pending row can still retry broker publication. Exhausted queued jobs show delivery_unconfirmed and require authorized operator reconciliation if all broker messages were lost.",
    "Cancellation is best effort at item boundaries and does not undo an external call already made.",
    "Langfuse remote export is opt-in and was not sent to a live service. Provider-free fixtures are not live-model quality, current-law coverage, legal correctness, production identity, capacity, or disaster-recovery evidence.",
    "The v0.7.0 tests prove observation serialization, redaction and failure isolation but not all production runtime fields required by MASTER_PLAN section 11.6. Correlated M2/M5 telemetry, real budget/retry/cache/evidence/model-usage/duration facts and truthful idempotent status events require the pending v0.7.1 patch.",
    "Alembic 0007 downgrade rejects nonempty M6 job history. Preserve PostgreSQL state and use a planned forward repair for valuable jobs; deleting Redis or database volumes is not rollback evidence."
  ],
